<%- /*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2

Caller of the shared scorecard run, as a consumer keeps it in
.github/workflows/scorecard-check.yml. The rendered file is the whole of the
consumer's scorecard job: the steps live in .github/workflows/scorecard.yml of
the shared repository, named here by commit with the version as a comment.

Public repositories only: the action asks the best-practices badge service
and the dependency insight service with the name of the repository. The
switch is therefore the repository's visibility, read on every run, and a
caller that passes a plain true is refused by tools/render.py (decision
record 0013). Render this file in a public repository only: in a private or
internal repository the switch is off, and a run that analyses nothing
fails, so "Scorecard / Analysis" is red with the reason in its text
(decision record 0026).

Not passed: `publish`. The Scorecard service reads the called workflow file
from the shared repository before it takes a result, which it can do only
once that repository is public.

Scopes: the job grants what the called job asks for and nothing else.
security-events write puts the findings into the forge's code scanning,
id-token write is used only when the result is published.

Required check: none. The job runs on a push to the default branch and on a
schedule, never on a pull request, and passes whatever it finds; the forge
reports it as "Scorecard / Public repository" and "Scorecard / Analysis" (the
first refuses a repository that is not public, decision record 0015; the
second fails when the switch is off, and the analysis job then reports as
"Scorecard / Analysis (not started)", decision record 0026). The engine declares a calling job under
its own name, which no run reports (cordanaLLM/praetor#1212), so the job stays
out of the consumer's required checks.

Fields: .Shared.Repository, .Shared.Commit and .Shared.Version are working
names until the engine renders caller templates (cordanaLLM/praetor#1211).
The trigger is spelled out for the same reason. The runner is no field: the
Scorecard service takes a result only from a job whose runner label is
written out, so the called workflow names it.

Concurrency is set here and not in the shared workflow, so a consumer's group
never collides with another caller's.

Licence header: the rendered caller starts with the consumer's own header,
written from .Licence (working names, as above), so the consumer's licence
check accepts it (#3). The REUSE-IgnoreStart and REUSE-IgnoreEnd notes render
as nothing and keep this repository's licence check from reading the field
lines as tags.
*/ -%>
<%- /* REUSE-IgnoreStart */ -%>
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: <% .Licence.CopyrightText %>
# SPDX-License-Identifier: <% .Licence.Identifier %>
<%/* REUSE-IgnoreEnd */ -%>
---
# Scorecard: the supply-chain checks of this repository, reported to code
# scanning. The job is the shared workflow of <% .Shared.Repository %>, named
# by commit. It runs in a public repository only.
name: Scorecard check

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  schedule:
    - cron: "23 4 * * 2"

permissions: {}

concurrency:
  group: scorecard-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

jobs:
  scorecard:
    name: Scorecard
    permissions:
      contents: read
      security-events: write # the findings go to the forge's code scanning
      id-token: write # asked for by the called job; used only for a publication
    uses: <% .Shared.Repository %>/.github/workflows/scorecard.yml@<% .Shared.Commit %> # <% .Shared.Version %>
    with:
      outside_hosts: ${{ github.event.repository.visibility == 'public' }}
